In this activity, we created a custom-format backup of the CampusSafe database using PostgreSQL’s pg_dump utility. We inspected the backup archive using pg_restore --list and restored it into a separate test database to avoid affecting the original database. We then checked the restored database to verify that the expected tables were present.

This process demonstrated the basic backup and restoration workflow and emphasized the importance of testing a backup in an isolated environment. It also highlighted the need to verify restored data, database objects, constraints, and access privileges before considering a recovery successful.    
